- D0 (before any model call): the Model D server runs with OCM_SCOPE=code, the setting the product's DEPLOY.md gives for bug reports. The server default (all) would include Django's large docs/ in readouts. The alone server's scope is irrelevant, since it is never asked for a readout. 2026-10-16T20:31:12+0530
- D1 (after the 3-question smoke test, before the full run): the alone arm cost $0.054 per question in the smoke test, so the $12 cap would stop it before Q4. The caps are now alone $16 and Model D $10. The smoke rows (k 4876-4878) are kept as the first rows of both arms. 2026-10-16T20:33:11+0530
- D2 (during Q1, before any later quarter): T5 as written is an identity. E and K measured on a quarter's own questions make (1-nu)E + nu*K equal that quarter's mean Model D cost, so the 'law' always matches. T5 is replaced, before Q2 data exist, by T5': for each quarter t >= 2, forecast the saving from E, K and A measured on all earlier quarters, with that quarter's observed nu_t; held if within 15% of the measured saving. The original T5 is still printed, and is labelled an identity. 2026-10-16T20:36:57+0530
- D3 (scheduling only): the alone arm's remaining questions run in 3 parallel shards (k mod 3), each writing rows_alone_s<i>.jsonl and skipping any k already in rows_alone*.jsonl. The alone arm never learns, so order cannot matter. Model D stays sequential. 2026-10-16T20:36:57+0530
- D4 (after 49 Model D questions, before the full results): the pre-registered rule for read-path answers (the readout's first file must be a changed file) misjudges reads. The reader often answers from a later item in the readout, and 4 of the first 6 read answers that the rule marks wrong name the changed file. The primary measure stays as pre-registered. A secondary measure, labelled 'cited', is added: a read-path answer is right if its text cites one of the changed files. Teach-path and alone answers keep their explicit 'at' location, so they score the same under both measures. 2026-10-16T20:42:57+0530
- D5 (with 110 of 288 alone questions done): the alone arm runs at $0.066 per question, so $16 would stop it near question 240 and leave Q4 thin. The cap is now $20, in 3 shards as before, resuming. 2026-10-16T20:46:12+0530
- D6: the gated arm lost k 4895 to one HTTP 500 from its workspace server during a call, which did not reproduce on replay. The product's hybrid loop lets a failing tool call end the whole question; the fix (a failed tool call returns its error to the model as text) goes into release 0.4.0, not into this run. Gated comparisons are paired, so they leave out k 4895. 2026-10-16T20:46:12+0530
- D7: the alone arm cost $0.089 per question on average, rising through the year, so its $20 stopped it with 64 questions left, mostly in Q4. The Model D arms also run above plan ($0.042 and $0.037 per question) and would stop near question 240. The caps are now alone $27, Model D $13, gated $12, so every arm covers the whole year. The Model D clients are restarted with the new cap. Their learning lives in the workspace servers, so order and state are unchanged, and each resumes at its next k. 2026-10-16T21:07:40+0530
